1
00:00:14,532 --> 00:00:15,574
In the early years,

2
00:00:15,575 --> 00:00:17,576
there were not enough people in Hawaii

3
00:00:17,577 --> 00:00:19,620
to plant and harvest the fields,

4
00:00:19,621 --> 00:00:21,080
and to run the mills.

5
00:00:21,081 --> 00:00:22,957
So thousands of others came.

6
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:24,167
Chinese.

7
00:00:24,501 --> 00:00:25,501
Portuguese.

8
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:26,794
Japanese.

9
00:00:27,003 --> 00:00:28,004
Filipinos.

10
00:00:28,797 --> 00:00:31,924
People of many cultures, races, traditions,

11
00:00:31,925 --> 00:00:34,051
brought here by higher wages,

12
00:00:34,052 --> 00:00:35,845
by better living standards...

13
00:00:36,596 --> 00:00:40,809
sometimes by a freedom
they could not find in their homeland.

14
00:01:35,113 --> 00:01:38,073
- No, do it this way.
- Okay, I'll collect the money now.

15
00:01:38,074 --> 00:01:39,909
Dad, I'm going.

16
00:01:42,412 --> 00:01:43,663
Jorge.

17
00:01:45,248 --> 00:01:47,667
- Are you resigning today?
- Dad...

18
00:01:48,543 --> 00:01:50,170
Nevermind.

19
00:01:51,212 --> 00:01:52,839
That miki looks delicious, Jorge.

20
00:01:53,923 --> 00:01:55,008
Yeah.

21
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,886
You look busy.

22
00:01:58,303 --> 00:02:00,764
Your dad's making us do a lot of things.
It's collection time.

23
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:02,932
Alright.

24
00:02:03,975 --> 00:02:05,267
Jorge!

25
00:02:05,268 --> 00:02:06,727
Give some miki to your grandpa!

26
00:02:06,728 --> 00:02:08,021
I have it here.

27
00:02:11,816 --> 00:02:12,983
Okay, go.

28
00:02:12,984 --> 00:02:13,984
Yes.

29
00:02:14,402 --> 00:02:16,237
- Make it quick.
- I'm on it.

30
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:21,910
- Good morning, Auntie!
- I saw your grandpa.

31
00:02:22,619 --> 00:02:24,412
He got there earlier than you.

32
00:02:25,121 --> 00:02:26,747
You're still here.

33
00:02:26,748 --> 00:02:29,375
You still jog even when it rains, Auntie?

34
00:02:29,376 --> 00:02:30,919
The rain stopped already.

35
00:02:31,378 --> 00:02:33,003
You know...

36
00:02:33,004 --> 00:02:36,257
If you really want to
inherit the restaurant

37
00:02:38,676 --> 00:02:41,428
you must get there before your grandpa.

38
00:02:41,429 --> 00:02:43,555
That's my plan, Auntie.

39
00:02:43,556 --> 00:02:48,311
I'm telling you, your dad will
come to his senses soon.

40
00:02:49,104 --> 00:02:51,730
- Take care, okay?
- Yes, Auntie.

41
00:02:51,731 --> 00:02:52,731
Take care.

42
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:07,000
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 1)

43
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,083
Ruth!

44
00:03:10,542 --> 00:03:11,835
Ugly Ruth!

45
00:03:12,127 --> 00:03:14,128
Ruth, you flirt!

46
00:03:14,129 --> 00:03:15,797
- Come out now.
- What?

47
00:03:16,756 --> 00:03:18,048
What?

48
00:03:18,049 --> 00:03:20,468
My god!

49
00:03:20,802 --> 00:03:23,303
- Don't rush me.
- Wow!

50
00:03:23,304 --> 00:03:24,264
What?

51
00:03:24,265 --> 00:03:25,807
Enough with the makeup.

52
00:03:26,182 --> 00:03:28,851
You'll always be single anyway.

53
00:03:28,852 --> 00:03:29,852
Oh.

54
00:03:29,853 --> 00:03:32,187
Go ahead...

55
00:03:32,188 --> 00:03:34,606
Tell all the neighbors!

56
00:03:34,607 --> 00:03:37,110
- Just hurry up.
- Wait, I'm coming.

57
00:03:41,906 --> 00:03:44,324
You're so slow.

58
00:03:44,325 --> 00:03:45,659
I said wait.

59
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,078
Wait!

60
00:03:50,498 --> 00:03:52,791
I'm here now.

61
00:03:52,792 --> 00:03:55,210
Stop it, you'll spill the miki.

62
00:03:55,211 --> 00:03:57,004
You should've brought some for me!

63
00:03:57,005 --> 00:03:59,549
You already ate so
much while I was cooking.

64
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,677
I didn't think there'd be any left.

65
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:05,012
You're so mean.

66
00:04:05,013 --> 00:04:07,306
Do I look like a pig to you?

67
00:04:07,307 --> 00:04:09,683
Ugh, keep up.

68
00:04:09,684 --> 00:04:11,226
Yes, boss.

69
00:04:11,227 --> 00:04:12,770
Right behind you.

70
00:04:13,062 --> 00:04:15,898
You're so slow.

71
00:04:15,899 --> 00:04:17,441
There are no more tricycles around

72
00:04:17,442 --> 00:04:19,651
and a lot of people are waiting.

73
00:04:19,652 --> 00:04:22,821
So what, it's my fault?

74
00:04:22,822 --> 00:04:24,616
Yes, it's your fault.

75
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,576
And why is that?

76
00:04:26,826 --> 00:04:28,494
You're too slow.

77
00:04:28,495 --> 00:04:30,579
Keep an eye out for passing tricycles.

78
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:31,873
Sure.

79
00:04:41,841 --> 00:04:42,841
Hey.

80
00:04:43,843 --> 00:04:45,677
Don't walk near the puddle.

81
00:04:45,678 --> 00:04:47,346
Do you want to get splashed with water?

82
00:04:47,347 --> 00:04:48,347
Oh,

83
00:04:48,431 --> 00:04:49,765
My bad.

84
00:04:49,766 --> 00:04:51,683
I didn't notice.

85
00:04:51,684 --> 00:04:55,521
Cutie said good morning to me.

86
00:04:55,522 --> 00:04:58,398
Who's Cutie?
Cutie can wait.

87
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:01,611
You wait. I'm still thinking of a reply.

88
00:05:04,155 --> 00:05:05,782
Who was that?!

89
00:05:06,115 --> 00:05:07,157
That guy's a jerk.

90
00:05:07,158 --> 00:05:09,452
Should we run after him?

91
00:05:11,037 --> 00:05:12,913
I hope you fall from your motorcycle!

92
00:05:12,914 --> 00:05:14,749
Idiot, we'll have you arrested!

93
00:05:15,458 --> 00:05:16,876
Look at your shirt.

94
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:19,962
Let's go home and change.

95
00:05:19,963 --> 00:05:21,255
Did you get his plate number?

96
00:05:21,256 --> 00:05:22,256
No, I didn't.

97
00:05:23,299 --> 00:05:26,009
But I'll recognize him
when I see him again.

98
00:05:26,010 --> 00:05:27,928
And then I'll punch him in the face.

99
00:05:27,929 --> 00:05:29,222
You're a mess.

100
00:05:31,099 --> 00:05:32,642
I'll just change at the restaurant.

101
00:05:33,101 --> 00:05:34,018
Look, there's a tricycle now.

102
00:05:34,018 --> 00:05:35,018
Hey!

103
00:06:29,741 --> 00:06:32,368
Good morning, Grandpa Tino.

104
00:06:33,786 --> 00:06:35,455
Why are you late?

105
00:06:36,164 --> 00:06:37,789
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

106
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:39,416
There weren't any tricycles around.

107
00:06:39,417 --> 00:06:44,504
There was a rude rider
that splashed mud on my shirt.

108
00:06:44,505 --> 00:06:48,258
I was thinking about what you said.

109
00:06:48,259 --> 00:06:50,928
The delivery app for the restaurant.

110
00:06:51,596 --> 00:06:54,098
Yes, Grandpa. Trust me.

111
00:06:54,641 --> 00:06:57,184
A lot of customers want deliveries.

112
00:06:57,185 --> 00:07:00,979
We need to be up to
date with social media and...

113
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,065
Enough.

114
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:05,150
There's an applicant already.

115
00:07:05,151 --> 00:07:06,402
Really?

116
00:07:07,111 --> 00:07:08,111
Yes!

117
00:07:09,822 --> 00:07:11,156
You'll be the one to interview him

118
00:07:11,157 --> 00:07:14,242
because I don't know anything
about social media.

119
00:07:14,243 --> 00:07:17,121
I have a doctor's appointment.

120
00:07:18,539 --> 00:07:20,457
But an applicant will come here later.

121
00:07:20,458 --> 00:07:21,458
I can do it, Grandpa.

122
00:07:21,459 --> 00:07:25,796
I'll tell him to manage
our social media pages

123
00:07:25,797 --> 00:07:29,300
as well as do the deliveries.

124
00:07:29,634 --> 00:07:31,510
Yes, everything you said.

125
00:07:31,511 --> 00:07:33,845
Do this well.

126
00:07:33,846 --> 00:07:37,350
Show me you can manage the restaurant.

127
00:07:38,059 --> 00:07:39,185
Thank you, Grandpa.

128
00:07:45,983 --> 00:07:47,067
Jorge!

129
00:07:47,068 --> 00:07:49,653
Wait, I'm changing my shirt.

130
00:07:49,654 --> 00:07:51,989
Do it faster and come here.

131
00:07:54,242 --> 00:07:55,409
What?

132
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:57,078
Did someone tell you already?

133
00:07:57,745 --> 00:08:00,664
That you look like Grandpa Tino
when he was young?

134
00:08:00,665 --> 00:08:02,457
Everyone says that.

135
00:08:02,458 --> 00:08:04,502
I told you, that's really me.

136
00:08:05,586 --> 00:08:07,254
That's why

137
00:08:07,255 --> 00:08:09,465
this restaurant is my destiny.

138
00:08:09,966 --> 00:08:12,802
Wow, that makes so much sense.

139
00:08:13,386 --> 00:08:15,263
You're both grumpy old men.

140
00:08:18,099 --> 00:08:18,975
Ruth.

141
00:08:18,976 --> 00:08:20,226
What?

142
00:08:21,121 --> 00:08:25,040
Has anybody told you that
you look like dinakdakan [choppped pork]?

143
00:08:25,064 --> 00:08:26,983
Damn you.

144
00:08:27,358 --> 00:08:29,276
Well, at least it's delicious.

145
00:08:29,277 --> 00:08:32,739
Oh, spoiled dinakdakan.

146
00:08:38,202 --> 00:08:40,704
Jorge, isn't that...

147
00:08:40,705 --> 00:08:42,915
You're right, it's him.

148
00:08:53,801 --> 00:08:56,261
Hey, he actually looks nice.

149
00:08:56,262 --> 00:08:58,805
Ruth, don't forget what he did.

150
00:08:58,806 --> 00:09:00,182
I can let go.

151
00:09:00,183 --> 00:09:02,893
Look, he's kind of cute.

152
00:09:02,894 --> 00:09:04,479
Stop that.

153
00:09:04,604 --> 00:09:06,354
Go wash in the kitchen.

154
00:09:06,355 --> 00:09:08,441
You're no fun.

155
00:09:11,986 --> 00:09:14,822
Sir, I'm here for a job.

156
00:09:19,786 --> 00:09:21,536
My name is Kiko Cablayan.

157
00:09:21,537 --> 00:09:24,164
I'm applying for the position
of social media manager

158
00:09:24,165 --> 00:09:25,666
and delivery boy.

159
00:09:38,721 --> 00:09:40,389
You don't recognize me?

160
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,852
Were we classmates in grade school?

161
00:09:45,853 --> 00:09:46,853
No.

162
00:09:47,522 --> 00:09:50,565
You splashed mud on me
on the way here.

163
00:09:50,566 --> 00:09:55,321
Oh, you're the ones waiting
in the middle of the road.

164
00:09:57,615 --> 00:09:59,075
I didn't mean to.

165
00:10:00,868 --> 00:10:03,412
Is the owner here?

166
00:10:05,331 --> 00:10:10,837
We don't accept crazy people here.

167
00:10:12,004 --> 00:10:13,214
How come?

168
00:10:13,881 --> 00:10:15,882
Are you the owner?

169
00:10:15,883 --> 00:10:16,968
No.

170
00:10:18,177 --> 00:10:19,678
Not yet.

171
00:10:19,679 --> 00:10:21,139
So, you're not.

172
00:10:21,889 --> 00:10:23,349
You're all talk.

173
00:10:23,850 --> 00:10:27,061
Did I do anything wrong, huh?

174
00:10:28,104 --> 00:10:29,355
You're fired.

175
00:10:30,189 --> 00:10:32,149
But I'm not hired yet.

176
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:37,113
Okay, fine.

177
00:10:39,448 --> 00:10:40,491
You're hired.

178
00:10:42,243 --> 00:10:43,369
You're fired!

179
00:10:43,911 --> 00:10:44,996
Get out.

180
00:10:45,413 --> 00:10:47,330
You're hired and then you're fired.

181
00:10:47,331 --> 00:10:50,585
You're not even the owner.

182
00:10:51,210 --> 00:10:53,628
What's going on here?

183
00:10:53,629 --> 00:10:54,672
Bong?

184
00:10:59,802 --> 00:11:03,763
Good morning, sir.
I'm Kiko Cablayan.

185
00:11:03,764 --> 00:11:05,641
Are you the applicant?

186
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,310
Yes, sir. Kiko.

187
00:11:08,311 --> 00:11:09,645
Where are you from?

188
00:11:09,979 --> 00:11:13,733
I'm from Cagayan but now I live in Ilocos.

189
00:11:14,483 --> 00:11:15,192
That's good.

190
00:11:15,193 --> 00:11:17,445
You can start right away.

191
00:11:18,529 --> 00:11:22,198
- We have a lot of deliveries.
- But Grandpa...

192
00:11:22,199 --> 00:11:26,244
And Kiko, I believe you will
do your best for this job.

193
00:11:26,245 --> 00:11:28,289
For sure, boss!

194
00:11:32,752 --> 00:11:34,629
Grandpa...

195
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:37,673
- Grandpa, wait.
- What now?

196
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:41,010
I bet this will fit you perfectly.

197
00:11:42,678 --> 00:11:43,803
Yes, sir.

198
00:11:43,804 --> 00:11:45,681
This is perfect.

199
00:11:47,767 --> 00:11:49,100
Kiko...

200
00:11:49,101 --> 00:11:55,649
Jorge will brief you about your tasks.

201
00:11:55,650 --> 00:11:56,650
Yes, sir.

202
00:11:57,234 --> 00:12:00,863
But he didn't pass...

203
00:12:01,781 --> 00:12:03,658
Grandpa!

204
00:12:09,664 --> 00:12:11,998
You already know how to manage
a social media page, right?

205
00:12:11,999 --> 00:12:13,960
I don't need to teach you?

206
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:16,378
Have you seen my social media profile?

207
00:12:16,379 --> 00:12:17,462
I saw it.

208
00:12:17,463 --> 00:12:18,965
Are you stalking me?

209
00:12:19,423 --> 00:12:20,548
Background check.

210
00:12:20,549 --> 00:12:22,718
That's what you call background check.

211
00:12:28,766 --> 00:12:31,142
Are you being the boss again?

212
00:12:31,143 --> 00:12:32,143
Yes.

213
00:12:34,772 --> 00:12:36,440
No.

214
00:12:38,651 --> 00:12:40,443
- Are you or are you not?
- I am.

215
00:12:40,444 --> 00:12:44,030
As long as Grandpa Tino
isn't here, I'm the boss.

216
00:12:44,031 --> 00:12:46,658
If he's here, he's the boss.

217
00:12:46,659 --> 00:12:49,036
But Boss Tino is here.

218
00:12:49,495 --> 00:12:50,495
He's not.

219
00:12:50,913 --> 00:12:52,289
He left.

220
00:12:54,208 --> 00:12:56,002
Okay, boss.

221
00:12:56,419 --> 00:12:57,837
Don't call me boss.

222
00:12:58,212 --> 00:12:59,505
You're making me look old.

223
00:13:00,339 --> 00:13:02,216
Then what? Jorge?

224
00:13:03,676 --> 00:13:05,386
How do you know my name?

225
00:13:05,928 --> 00:13:07,263
I heard it earlier.

226
00:13:08,222 --> 00:13:09,724
Are you stalking me?

227
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,853
Background check.

228
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:20,358
You'll do everything
for the social media page.

229
00:13:20,359 --> 00:13:24,279
You'll answer the queries

230
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:27,908
and you'll also deliver.

231
00:13:28,826 --> 00:13:30,618
Understood?

232
00:13:30,619 --> 00:13:32,079
Yes, Jorge.

233
00:13:32,455 --> 00:13:34,248
Are we friends now?

234
00:13:36,375 --> 00:13:37,543
No.

235
00:13:39,378 --> 00:13:40,796
Jorge!

236
00:15:12,858 --> 00:15:14,609
Come to work early tomorrow, okay?

237
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,183
Get home safe.

238
00:15:16,767 --> 00:15:17,767
Jorge!

239
00:15:17,845 --> 00:15:19,304
I'll drive you home.

240
00:15:20,104 --> 00:15:21,729
Right on time!
My feet hurt already.

241
00:15:21,730 --> 00:15:23,399
Wait, I'll get my helmet.

242
00:15:23,774 --> 00:15:24,774
Ruth...

243
00:15:24,859 --> 00:15:26,110
Jorge, come on.

244
00:15:28,404 --> 00:15:29,571
Come on.

245
00:15:29,572 --> 00:15:30,447
I don't want to.

246
00:15:30,448 --> 00:15:32,198
You're being stubborn again.

247
00:15:32,199 --> 00:15:33,408
You can't make me.

248
00:15:33,409 --> 00:15:34,409
Come on!

249
00:15:35,286 --> 00:15:36,287
Come on!

250
00:15:37,454 --> 00:15:41,125
Stop it, Ruth.
I said no.

251
00:15:49,049 --> 00:15:52,052
- Stop it, Ruth.
- It's so fun!

252
00:15:54,263 --> 00:15:56,181
You should've made me sit
in the middle.

253
00:15:56,182 --> 00:15:57,515
Why?

254
00:15:57,516 --> 00:15:59,058
So, I could eat your hair?

255
00:15:59,059 --> 00:16:01,812
You're such a crybaby.
That's why there's a helmet.

256
00:16:03,355 --> 00:16:06,149
It's a good thing
your cousin's helmet fit Jorge's head.

257
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:07,901
Focus on the road!

258
00:16:07,902 --> 00:16:10,195
Look at Jorge's head, it's so big.

259
00:16:10,196 --> 00:16:11,113
Right?

260
00:16:11,114 --> 00:16:12,448
Oh really?

261
00:16:13,157 --> 00:16:14,407
I swear if it gets bumpy,

262
00:16:14,408 --> 00:16:17,619
watch out, I'll push you.

263
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:19,787
Hold me tightly...

264
00:16:19,788 --> 00:16:22,499
...so you won't fall.

265
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:26,128
Ruth, stop it!

266
00:16:26,670 --> 00:16:28,087
Go faster.

267
00:16:28,088 --> 00:16:30,256
I want to go home already.

268
00:16:30,257 --> 00:16:31,257
Why?

269
00:16:31,258 --> 00:16:32,801
Are we friends now?

270
00:16:34,803 --> 00:16:37,305
You're just giving us a ride,

271
00:16:37,306 --> 00:16:38,973
what do you mean we're friends now?

272
00:16:38,974 --> 00:16:40,642
You're not that lucky.

273
00:16:40,643 --> 00:16:42,937
Just asking.

274
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:48,524
Ruth, are you having fun?

275
00:16:48,525 --> 00:16:51,320
Yes! Go faster!

276
00:17:06,085 --> 00:17:08,044
What's going on, Auntie?

277
00:17:08,045 --> 00:17:10,463
Jorge, your grandpa.

278
00:17:10,464 --> 00:17:11,547
What happened?

279
00:17:11,548 --> 00:17:13,258
The ambulance just left.

280
00:17:13,259 --> 00:17:16,220
Your father said to meet them
at the hospital.

281
00:17:17,221 --> 00:17:18,055
But how?

282
00:17:18,056 --> 00:17:22,685
Ask your friend
to give you a ride to Laoag.

283
00:17:24,103 --> 00:17:26,105
Auntie, what do you mean?

284
00:17:27,982 --> 00:17:29,984
Just ask your friend.

285
00:17:30,234 --> 00:17:32,236
Auntie...

286
00:17:32,736 --> 00:17:35,239
He was still okay at the restaurant.

287
00:17:36,198 --> 00:17:37,740
Why? How?

288
00:17:37,741 --> 00:17:39,326
Why would he be rushed to the hospital?

289
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:41,953
What did he do yesterday?

290
00:17:41,954 --> 00:17:44,248
I don't know.
He was in bed the whole afternoon.

291
00:17:44,665 --> 00:17:45,791
What did he eat?

292
00:17:46,250 --> 00:17:48,501
He ate rice.
He was still strong yesterday.

293
00:17:48,502 --> 00:17:50,754
And he was still strong earlier.

294
00:17:52,214 --> 00:17:55,592
I don't know about grandpa.
I don't know.

295
00:18:12,192 --> 00:18:13,276
Ruth.

296
00:18:13,277 --> 00:18:14,694
Stay here.

297
00:18:14,695 --> 00:18:15,778
Take care, okay?

298
00:18:15,779 --> 00:18:16,905
I will.

299
00:18:31,295 --> 00:18:35,466
- Ruth, take charge here.
- Yes.

300
00:18:46,185 --> 00:18:47,852
Dear Bong,

301
00:18:47,853 --> 00:18:52,732
I always think of what will happen.

302
00:18:52,733 --> 00:19:00,239
Will things fall into place
or will we always be like this?

303
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,867
always unsure

304
00:19:02,868 --> 00:19:07,331
always dreading
if this is all that the world has for us...

305
00:19:41,323 --> 00:19:43,325
Bong.

306
00:19:44,743 --> 00:19:47,996
Are we going to Hawaii?

307
00:19:57,423 --> 00:20:00,508
How about you, Bong?

308
00:20:00,509 --> 00:20:04,804
Do you also ask yourself
what will happen to us in the future?

309
00:20:04,805 --> 00:20:08,724
Who are we going to be?

310
00:20:08,725 --> 00:20:10,476
Where are we going to be?

311
00:20:10,477 --> 00:20:13,354
What do our future selves look like?

312
00:20:13,355 --> 00:20:15,606
Will things get better?

313
00:20:15,607 --> 00:20:17,900
Will our problems end?

314
00:20:17,901 --> 00:20:22,364
Will the world become
a better place for us?

315
00:20:34,251 --> 00:20:36,462
Kiko...

316
00:20:41,341 --> 00:20:43,343
Thank you.

317
00:20:49,641 --> 00:20:52,186
We're friends now.

318
00:20:59,151 --> 00:21:00,778
Jorge, my helmet...
